-- SCOPE (binding, ledger L8at): the RETURNED / WIRED theorems `topshare2.epD2M_returned` and `topshare2.epD2M_wired` that the opt-in shared-leaf CANDIDATE
-- (`Tools/ShippingSeqParentGenD2MS.lean`, `set_option sparkle.sharedLeafCandidate true`, default false) now generates in addition to `epD2M_endpoint`
-- (the generic `Tools.ShippingQuadReturned.quad_returned` / `quad_wired` applied to the generated data facts and the generated per-callee blocks).  The declaration
-- `topshare2` is generated by `Tests/Compiler/SharedLeafGenTest.lean`.  Here: (1) the FULL forall-type of each (outer binders: the entries, `JQC O 0 w`, the form of the run `h`, and
-- the whole conclusion) is compared by `isDefEq` with a HAND-WRITTEN statement (`Share2Ret`, `Share2Wired`, independent of the generator and of the generic theorems);
-- type-correct mutations (start world `JQC O 1 w`, `h` for another declaration, the entry of the second callee for the first, the conjunct `y.2 = Dg` replaced by `True`,
-- `DesignSemConcl` of `Dg` instead of `y.2`) are REJECTED; (2) a closure audit.  CONCRETE example (`topshare2` only), not whole-class coverage; the other premises
-- stay premises: `O`, `T`, `hA`, `MachineDefines` of the parent / callees / leaf, `JQC O 0 w`, the run `h`; `RealChildA` / `JQC` are histories, not freshness or semantic correctness.
-- No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`.
